WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:03.082
We turn to that murder mystery
that has gripped Canada.

00:00:03.082 --> 00:00:05.209
It did seem like you were watching

00:00:05.209 --> 00:00:07.337
a work of fiction, not reality.

00:00:07.337 --> 00:00:09.756
Tonight the mystery deepening behind

00:00:09.756 --> 00:00:13.009
the double homicide of one of
the world's richest couples.

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:16.137
But of course truth is often
much stranger than fiction

00:00:16.137 --> 00:00:18.473
as I learned as I went
on with the reporting.

00:00:18.473 --> 00:00:20.933
Their murder has shaken
the political establishment

00:00:20.933 --> 00:00:22.727
with many wondering who could have wanted

00:00:22.727 --> 00:00:24.937
to see them dead and why.

00:00:24.937 --> 00:00:29.817
This was just a seismic
event in the history

00:00:29.817 --> 00:00:32.487
of Canadian business and Canadian news.

00:00:32.487 --> 00:00:35.323
Now police want to know
who would want them dead.

00:00:35.323 --> 00:00:37.909
We are now well over a
year after their deaths

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:39.702
and they remain completely unsolved.

00:00:45.917 --> 00:00:49.420
It's quite a macabre story
in terms of how

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:51.130
Barry and Honey Sherman were discovered.

00:00:52.006 --> 00:00:56.719
They were last seen, both of
them, on December 13, 2018

00:00:56.719 --> 00:00:57.887
which was a Wednesday.

00:00:57.887 --> 00:01:00.181
They were trying to sell their home

00:01:00.181 --> 00:01:03.059
and so their real estate
agent was holding viewings

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:07.188
for prospective buyers
and the agent had a couple

00:01:07.188 --> 00:01:09.899
touring the home who were being shown

00:01:09.899 --> 00:01:11.859
around the kitchen, the bedrooms,

00:01:11.859 --> 00:01:14.278
and they were shown the indoor pool.

00:01:15.196 --> 00:01:18.908
If you can imagine a line of
people comes into the pool area

00:01:18.908 --> 00:01:22.829
and sees this really
gruesome tableau of

00:01:22.829 --> 00:01:26.624
Barry and Honey Sherman
suspended from a metal railing

00:01:26.624 --> 00:01:28.709
that surrounded one end of the pool

00:01:28.709 --> 00:01:31.254
with leather belts holding
them up by the neck.

00:01:32.814 --> 00:01:36.526
They were in kneeling positions
facing away from the water.

00:01:36.518 --> 00:01:38.806
She was kind of slumped
on her side a little bit,

00:01:38.806 --> 00:01:40.133
he was more upright.

00:01:40.969 --> 00:01:43.054
There was then a 911 call

00:01:43.054 --> 00:01:46.600
and the police were on the
scene very soon afterward.

00:01:46.708 --> 00:01:48.643
Now the billionaire
founder of Canada's largest

00:01:48.643 --> 00:01:51.479
drugs firm, Barry Sherman
and his wife Honey have been

00:01:51.476 --> 00:01:53.366
found dead at their home in Toronto.

00:01:53.366 --> 00:01:55.225
Police describe the deaths as suspicious

00:01:55.225 --> 00:01:57.811
but say they were not
being treated as murder.

00:01:57.811 --> 00:02:00.921
We discovered two bodies of
people inside a home here.

00:02:00.921 --> 00:02:03.799
The circumstances of their
death appear suspicious.

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:05.259
Homicide detectives are leading

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:07.660
the investigation but there
is still no indication

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:10.537
from police that the deaths are homicides.

00:02:11.576 --> 00:02:14.120
Over the next 24 hours you began to see

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.521
anonymously sourced stories in some of the

00:02:16.521 --> 00:02:19.089
Toronto papers to the
effect that the police

00:02:19.089 --> 00:02:21.514
were treating this as a murder-suicide

00:02:21.514 --> 00:02:23.182
committed by Barry Sherman.

00:02:24.321 --> 00:02:26.722
The Sherman's adult
children put out a statement

00:02:26.722 --> 00:02:28.622
saying that this was
completely inconsistent

00:02:28.622 --> 00:02:30.773
with the character of their parents

00:02:30.773 --> 00:02:33.275
and they also put together
their own investigative team.

00:02:33.275 --> 00:02:36.594
And they actually did a second
autopsy which is remarkable.

00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:39.889
They found things that
they believed indicated

00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:41.730
this could not have been a murder-suicide,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:44.339
narrow markings on Barry Sherman's wrists,

00:02:44.339 --> 00:02:47.574
the scene was for lack of
a better word, quite clean,

00:02:47.574 --> 00:02:49.499
the way in which the murder scene

00:02:49.499 --> 00:02:50.958
seemed to have been staged.

00:02:51.997 --> 00:02:53.480
And then in late January

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.631
the police hold a press conference.

00:02:55.631 --> 00:02:59.992
We believe now through the
six weeks of work review,

00:02:59.992 --> 00:03:02.894
we have sufficient
evidence to describe this

00:03:02.894 --> 00:03:05.921
as a double homicide investigation

00:03:05.921 --> 00:03:09.966
and that both Honey and Barry
Sherman were in fact targeted.

00:03:09.966 --> 00:03:13.517
We are not police
detectives, we do not have access

00:03:13.517 --> 00:03:16.127
to the corpus of evidence,
we are not going to solve

00:03:16.127 --> 00:03:19.487
the crime, so my goal was
create the richest portrait

00:03:19.487 --> 00:03:22.305
possible of this very unusual person

00:03:22.305 --> 00:03:25.099
and how he came to this very unusual end.

00:03:25.461 --> 00:03:26.676
As head of Apotex,

00:03:26.676 --> 00:03:29.267
the largest pharmaceutical
company in Canada,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.174
Barry's net worth was estimated

00:03:31.174 --> 00:03:34.343
at over $4 billion at
the time of his death.

00:03:35.825 --> 00:03:38.083
Barry Sherman was a science guy.

00:03:38.083 --> 00:03:43.034
He had a PhD in physics
at MIT but he had become

00:03:43.034 --> 00:03:46.974
an expert in generics and in drugs.

00:03:46.995 --> 00:03:50.671
The generics business is a very tough one.

00:03:50.671 --> 00:03:55.234
It is zero sum in the
strictest sense of the term.

00:03:55.239 --> 00:03:57.931
That means that if you're selling 
a branded drug

00:03:57.931 --> 00:04:00.981
you have had a significant
amount of your profit wiped out

00:04:00.981 --> 00:04:04.282
and he was very tough in doing
this, very uncompromising.

00:04:04.282 --> 00:04:05.831
When you speak to people in the

00:04:05.831 --> 00:04:08.547
branded pharmaceutical
industry they sometimes refer

00:04:08.547 --> 00:04:11.133
to Barry Sherman in unprintable terms.

00:04:13.772 --> 00:04:16.775
It has been said, though
there may be some exaggeration

00:04:16.775 --> 00:04:18.782
in the numbers, that he
would sometimes be involved

00:04:18.782 --> 00:04:21.785
in as many as 100
lawsuits at any one time.

00:04:21.785 --> 00:04:25.044
He was a guy who did
not like to be crossed

00:04:25.044 --> 00:04:27.552
and if someone did betray
him or did something

00:04:27.552 --> 00:04:31.562
that he felt was improper
or disloyal, he would sue.

00:04:31.562 --> 00:04:32.819
He was a tough guy.

00:04:32.819 --> 00:04:36.328
Definitely someone who did
not have a lot of friends

00:04:36.328 --> 00:04:38.038
beyond his inner circle.

00:04:38.074 --> 00:04:40.916
Barry Sherman did face multiple lawsuits,

00:04:40.916 --> 00:04:43.668
among them a decade long
battle with a group of cousins

00:04:43.668 --> 00:04:45.962
who felt cut out of the Sherman business.

00:04:47.005 --> 00:04:48.762
These murders had sort of a

00:04:48.762 --> 00:04:51.484
Murder On The Orient Express quality to them.

00:04:51.484 --> 00:04:53.951
There was a long list
of theories out there.

00:04:53.951 --> 00:04:56.250
Someone who everyone
looked at very quickly

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.764
was Barry Sherman's cousin, Kerry Winter,

00:04:58.764 --> 00:05:02.565
the son of Lewis Winter, the
founder of Empire Laboratories,

00:05:02.565 --> 00:05:05.651
the company where Barry
worked as a student

00:05:05.651 --> 00:05:07.987
and later ended up owning and Kerry

00:05:07.987 --> 00:05:10.620
and his siblings have been
engaged in a legal battle

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:13.707
alleging that he owes them 20% of Apotex,

00:05:13.707 --> 00:05:16.048
that they were done out
of their inheritance.

00:05:16.048 --> 00:05:22.763
He cared about one thing,
money, making lots of it

00:05:22.763 --> 00:05:26.350
and not caring who he
destroyed, who he stepped on.

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:29.895
That is a very bitter legal
battle and it's one where

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:33.816
Kerry has expressed publicly
and otherwise a lot of anger,

00:05:34.213 --> 00:05:37.133
said some things that certainly did not

00:05:37.133 --> 00:05:38.885
make him less of a suspect.

00:05:38.885 --> 00:05:43.890
I probably had reasons to lash
out, to do the dirty deed.

00:05:45.082 --> 00:05:48.669
But here he is, over a
year later, walking free

00:05:48.669 --> 00:05:51.011
and unarrested so I think it's safe to say

00:05:51.011 --> 00:05:53.680
that he had nothing to do with this.

00:05:53.752 --> 00:05:55.343
Police say they are still talking

00:05:55.343 --> 00:05:57.970
to neighbors, witnesses, family members,

00:05:57.970 --> 00:06:00.806
business associates,
anyone who knew anything

00:06:00.806 --> 00:06:04.101
about the Sherman's lives
or even their last hours.

00:06:04.101 --> 00:06:06.729
One of the things I was astounded by

00:06:06.729 --> 00:06:08.856
when I started reporting this story,

00:06:08.856 --> 00:06:11.526
and it's something that I
really had no inkling of,

00:06:11.526 --> 00:06:16.447
was the extent of some of
Barry Sherman's entanglements

00:06:16.447 --> 00:06:23.168
with really inadvisable
financial deals, businesses,

00:06:23.168 --> 00:06:26.546
and this put him in to bed
financially with a lot of people

00:06:26.546 --> 00:06:30.467
who really most high level
pharmaceutical executives

00:06:30.467 --> 00:06:32.761
would never have anything to do with.

00:06:33.992 --> 00:06:37.287
Kevin Trudeau, now in jail,
another convicted fraudster

00:06:37.287 --> 00:06:39.957
called Shaun Rootenberg
convinced Barry Sherman

00:06:39.957 --> 00:06:42.709
to invest in a online trivia app.

00:06:42.709 --> 00:06:44.670
The introduction in that case was made

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.136
by someone called Myron Gottlieb.

00:06:47.136 --> 00:06:49.472
Gottlieb and Rootenberg
had actually met in jail

00:06:49.472 --> 00:06:51.891
and the most dramatic
of these involvements

00:06:51.891 --> 00:06:54.852
over the years was someone
named Frank D'Angelo.

00:06:55.634 --> 00:06:58.887
He is something of a B-list 
celebrity in Canada.

00:06:58.887 --> 00:07:02.390
He's well known as a director of movies

00:07:02.390 --> 00:07:04.679
that don't typically get great reviews.

00:07:06.341 --> 00:07:08.469
Barry Sherman invested
in most of these films.

00:07:08.469 --> 00:07:09.636
&lt;i&gt;Do what you gotta do.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:15.339 --> 00:07:16.757
&lt;i&gt;You're trouble for me Angelo.&lt;/i&gt;

00:07:17.692 --> 00:07:23.364
I met Frank for lunch
and he is a colorful guy

00:07:23.364 --> 00:07:24.490
to say the least.

00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:26.576
If you wanna talk about
unprintable language,

00:07:26.576 --> 00:07:28.578
he certainly uses a lot of it.

00:07:28.578 --> 00:07:31.956
I just felt that I owed it to Barry

00:07:31.956 --> 00:07:33.916
to give my two cents.

00:07:34.097 --> 00:07:36.663
You know I don't think
I'll ever get over this

00:07:37.495 --> 00:07:42.653
incredible tragedy, this senseless act,

00:07:42.658 --> 00:07:45.250
as long as I live on this planet.

00:07:45.646 --> 00:07:47.985
You can see the appeal
of hanging out with him

00:07:47.985 --> 00:07:50.070
for Barry, particularly
because he would've been

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:53.240
so dramatically different
from the other people

00:07:53.240 --> 00:07:55.492
who Barry Sherman would've seen

00:07:55.492 --> 00:07:57.536
and dealt with on a daily basis.

00:07:57.536 --> 00:07:59.663
Meeting Frank was not
uncomfortable at all.

00:07:59.663 --> 00:08:02.372
He was happy to help,
he had checked me out.

00:08:03.326 --> 00:08:04.953
He knew about me.

00:08:04.953 --> 00:08:08.172
I think I found him on
Facebook and sent him a note

00:08:08.172 --> 00:08:11.246
asking if he would meet and
after a few days he responded

00:08:11.282 --> 00:08:12.453
and said that he would.

00:08:12.453 --> 00:08:15.290
But he did make clear to me,
he pulled me close as we were

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:17.709
leaving that first
lunch, and said you know,

00:08:17.709 --> 00:08:18.960
do the right thing for my friend

00:08:18.960 --> 00:08:21.754
and if you don't I'm gonna
come to London and find you.

00:08:21.831 --> 00:08:24.667
He had been questioned by the police.

00:08:24.667 --> 00:08:27.844
He is emphatic that he had
nothing to do with the murder

00:08:27.844 --> 00:08:31.306
but he is of course
emblematic, indicative,

00:08:31.306 --> 00:08:35.602
of the tone of some of these
financial entanglements

00:08:35.602 --> 00:08:39.898
and those entanglements are to
many people very suspicious.

00:08:43.190 --> 00:08:44.994
Hank Idsinga, the acting inspector

00:08:44.994 --> 00:08:47.041
of the homicide squad,
says the investigation into

00:08:47.041 --> 00:08:50.336
who killed Barry and Honey
Sherman is still very active.

00:08:50.336 --> 00:08:52.464
I feel for the family and the friends.

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:55.216
It's dragging on, it has been a year.

00:08:56.022 --> 00:09:00.485
As an attempt to reignite an investigation,

00:09:00.829 --> 00:09:05.083
The Sherman family has asked
me to announce the offer

00:09:05.083 --> 00:09:11.297
of a reward of up to $10
million dollars for information leading

00:09:11.297 --> 00:09:14.882
to the apprehension and
prosecution of those responsible

00:09:14.882 --> 00:09:16.717
for the murders of
Honey and Barry Sherman.

00:09:16.919 --> 00:09:18.504
Truth is very strange, you know.

00:09:18.504 --> 00:09:19.922
Truth is much stranger than fiction,

00:09:19.922 --> 00:09:22.261
that's why I love this job,
is that you keep finding out

00:09:22.261 --> 00:09:25.441
that what happens in the
real world is just as weird

00:09:25.441 --> 00:09:28.736
or weirder than Hollywood
could every come up with.

00:09:29.956 --> 00:09:34.846
It seems pretty clear to
all involved that something

00:09:34.846 --> 00:09:37.933
that Barry Sherman got
involved in went wrong

00:09:37.933 --> 00:09:40.268
and came back at him.

00:09:40.602 --> 00:09:44.106
If you think about the crime,
it is remarkable in many ways.

00:09:44.106 --> 00:09:46.274
One of the things that's
remarkable is that

00:09:46.274 --> 00:09:49.364
his wife was killed and the
other thing that I think

00:09:49.364 --> 00:09:51.450
has confounded a lot of the investigators

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:54.369
is when there are hits,
it's usually a bullet,

00:09:54.369 --> 00:09:57.918
it's usually quick, it's
done cleanly, efficiently,

00:09:57.918 --> 00:09:59.837
in a way that allows a quick getaway.

00:10:01.199 --> 00:10:03.507
Barry and Honey Sherman
were strangled to death.

00:10:03.507 --> 00:10:07.514
So there's this confusing
tangle of evidence

00:10:07.514 --> 00:10:10.187
that for the police and
for anyone else trying

00:10:10.187 --> 00:10:13.114
to understand this, it doesn't
all point in one direction

00:10:13.114 --> 00:10:17.914
and that's I think what is
so tantalizing about this

00:10:17.914 --> 00:10:20.500
as a mystery in some way
and I think it's a mystery

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:21.918
that's going to endure.

